### Step 4 — Profile, avatar, preferences, public profile. VS Code "REST Client".
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Sign up a fresh user
# @name signup
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "profile_chef", "email": "profile_chef@cookify.dev", "password": "Cookify2026!", "confirmPassword": "Cookify2026!" }

### 2. Update profile → 200
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{signup.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "profile_chef",
  "firstName": "Priya",
  "lastName": "Sharma",
  "phone": "+919812345678",
  "age": 29,
  "gender": "FEMALE",
  "bio": "Weekend baker and dal enthusiast.",
  "preferredLang": "en"
}

### 3. Invalid values → 400 with field errors (age, bio, language)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{signup.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "profile_chef", "age": 10, "preferredLang": "de" }

### 4. Upload avatar (multipart). Put any image next to this file as avatar.jpg.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me/avatar
Authorization: Bearer {{signup.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=CookifyBoundary

--CookifyBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="avatar.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./avatar.jpg
--CookifyBoundary--

### 5. Set dietary preferences
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me/preferences
Authorization: Bearer {{signup.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "dietType": "JAIN", "maxCalories": 650, "minProtein": 25 }

### 6. Read preferences back
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me/preferences
Authorization: Bearer {{signup.response.body.accessToken}}

### 7. Public profile — no login needed, no email/phone in the response
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/profile_chef

### 8. Unknown user → 404 USER_NOT_FOUND
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/nobody_here
